reproduced locally. go's json.Marshal with `omitempty` on a string removes empty string fields. Minimal repro:

```go
package main
import (
  "encoding/json"
  "fmt"
)

type ToolArgs struct {
  Query string `json:"query"`
  Kind  string `json:"kind,omitempty"`
}

func main() {
  t := ToolArgs{Query: "accounts.csv", Kind: ""}
  b, _ := json.Marshal(t)
  fmt.Println(string(b)) // prints {"query":"accounts.csv"}
}
```

looks like go-sdk codegen started emitting `omitempty` for union/discriminator fields in v0.9.7 -> v0.9.8 to reduce payload size. That's incorrect for discriminators — missing vs empty has semantics at our routing layer.

filing PR for codegen change + unit test (will link PR when ready). Also adding a test in go-sdk CI to ensure discriminator isn't omitted when empty string provided.
